fe.add_exercise(S, 'ownership and authorization', """Assets have an `owner` text but no notion of who may change them. Add `X-Actor` as the borrower/custodian: `POST` stamps `custodian`; `PUT`/`PATCH`/`DELETE` require the custodian (403, row and activity unchanged); reads stay open; missing header on writes is 401. Write the test first.""", """Reference: an actor middleware; `custodian` column; in the `PATCH /status` transaction compare `current.rows[0].custodian` with `req.actor` after the `FOR UPDATE` and throw a `ForbiddenError` (403) before the `UPDATE`.

Review: the comparison is on the locked, committed row; explain why the `owner` display field must not be used for this."""); done.append('2.5 ownership/authz exercise 7 (05, 06)')
